{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794752406,"nonce":"7IrgoiKz3NiQVy8kGjQ0A0s9WIU=","message":"Threads for hxcpp through Emscripten (user, 2026-11-15: hxn can give them through krio). hxn-future already runs stepped work on a krio_parallel Cluster where the build has threads (63d7739). Under Emscripten that Cluster can run on Web Workers with krio-wasm: parking is core wasm atomics, the host supplies an agent spawn hook (Emscripten's pthread Workers) and the epoch clock. Needs a shared-memory build throughout (std through build-std with +atomics,+bulk-memory, the library, hxcpp linked with -pthread) and a cross-origin-isolated page (COOP/COEP); without either, keep the single-thread stepped driver, as krio-wasm's cluster_support says to. The page's main thread still cannot block, so await stays unusable there; -sPROXY_TO_PTHREAD runs main on a Worker, where await works and WebGPU is reached through an OffscreenCanvas. To do: an hxn build mode for it (hxn build cpp --wasm --threads, say), krio-wasm's spawn hook over Emscripten's workers, the COOP/COEP headers on emrun's server (it has none; hxn would serve the page itself or pass headers), and the counter fixture's concurrent futures run that way.","files":null}]}